<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">4 events that happened on 22 November, from 1220 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1220 CE <span class="tih-ago">806 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick II is crowned Holy Roman Emperor in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a> crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> emperor in St Peter's. Brilliant and controversial, the 'wonder of the world' ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and spent much of his reign in conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honorius">Honorius</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1497 CE <span class="tih-ago">529 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vasco da Gama rounds the Cape of Good Hope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a>'s Portuguese fleet rounded the southern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> on its way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. The voyage opened a direct sea route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and the rise of a Portuguese trading empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1963 CE <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President Kennedy is assassinated in Dallas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John F. Kennedy was shot dead while riding in an open motorcade through Dealey Plaza in Dallas. Vice-President Lyndon Johnson was sworn in aboard Air Force One the same afternoon.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1975 CE <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Juan Carlos is proclaimed king of Spain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after Franco's death, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-carlos-i">Juan Carlos de Borbón</a> was proclaimed king. Expected to preserve the dictatorship, he instead guided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s transition to a parliamentary democracy.</p></div></li></ol>
